Share member suffixes through monotone maps

Avoid copying every transported member row when an increasing element
map can preserve a shared tree level. Compress contiguous source and
target IDs into offset runs, and use inverse lookup so gaps do not
force a tree scan.

Share the final mapped column and its unchanged suffix. Earlier mapped
columns rebuild their prefixes because their values need transformation.
Keep sparse image updates map-driven and avoid preparing large maps for
small source deltas so incremental updates do not require full scans.

Transport member suffixes as relations, retaining all images for
partial, non-monotone, and temporarily non-functional maps. Keep
canonicalization unchanged so equality merges continue to restore
canonical rows.

Cover offset runs, shared snapshots, conflicting images, late map
growth, and source and target equality changes with runtime and
evaluator tests.

Validation: runtime, evaluator, and compile test suites pass. The
member mapping and morphism preservation cases also pass in native
and desugared models with naive and semi-naive evaluation. Formatting
and patch checks pass.
